# Anything a Linux container executes must be LF in the WORKING TREE, not just
# in the repository.
#
# git stores these with LF already, so Render -- which builds from the git
# checkout -- has always worked. But core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrites
# them to CRLF on checkout, and `docker build` copies the WORKING TREE. So a
# local container build baked a CRLF entrypoint and died with
#
#     /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# or, worse, parsed far enough to pass "$PORT\r" to uvicorn. The deploy path
# and the local path disagreed, and only the local one was broken -- which is
# why it went unnoticed.
#
# After adding this, existing checkouts need `git add --renormalize .` once.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
